        <p>Botterill, curate of St. Andrew's, Eccles. The Vicar took the opening part of the service, and Psalm xc. was chanted by the AO choir. The hymn, "Father of Heaven, Whose love profound," was next sung, and then the Vicar read the lesson. After the hymn "Abide with me " had been sung with much feeling, the prayers of the service were taken by the Vicar of St. Andrews Fccles. As the coffin was borne from the church the Detel March from "Saul" was played, and committal sentences nod prayers were read i at the graveside by the Rev. H. J. B. Armstrong.</p>
