      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-08-01_WidnesExaminer_art0020" n="art0020">
        <head>WARRINGTON BURGLARY.</head>
        <p>A WARRINGTON BURGLARY.</p>
        <p>Joinnary In a Spout.</p>
        <p>At Warrington rclice Court en Saturday, James Biggins, labourer, was charged with Lreaking and entering the shop of Samuel Fernley, jeweller, 71, Bridge-street, the previous Saturday morning, and stealing a quantity of cold bracelets and alberts. James Ready and Elizabeth Ready were charged nith receiving the properly, knowing it to have been stolen. Superintendent Monaghan stated that an examination of the shop showed that nn entrance Lad been effected by climbinc over a high wall at the rear of the premises and breaking a window cn the ground floor: About three o'clock in the morning a lodging-house keeper named tiogerson saw Higgins scaling a wall, and be afterwards heard a smash of gla s. The police were informed, and from statements made by Higgins at the police station rfsearch was mnde at the House of Ready, mho is brother-in-law of Higgins. On search- ing the house seine of the stolen jenellery was found concealed in one of the spouts. Other jewellery was traced to having hcen disposed of by the female prisoner to different women in the neizbbourl,cod. The magistrates ccimuitted the irisoner to the Liverpool Quarter Scssicus.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-08-01_WidnesExaminer_art0021" n="art0021">
        <head>Drunk on Licensed Premises.</head>
        <p>Drunk on Licensed Premises.</p>
        <p>Pra,trick Carey, Scotland-road, was charged at the o lice Court on Tuesday with having been drunk on the licensed premises if the Rcel.uck Hotel, Bridge- street, at 7 -15 on Monday night.—P.C. Hewitt said he was in oompany with P.C. Tolley when he saw prisoner, who was drunk, enter the Roebuck Hotel. He requested him to leave, but he refused, and he had to lock him up. Prisoner also used bad language. Prisoner said he did not go into the house, and he eid not use bad language.—Fined ss. and ccsts (Sc. Bd.-.</p>
      </div>
