      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-08-01_WidnesExaminer_art0113" n="art0113">
        <head>BOWLING.</head>
        <p>BOWLING.</p>
        <p>THE CROSFIELD CUP.</p>
        <p>-- YORKSHIRE v. LANCASHIRE AND CH ESHIRE</p>
        <p>TV's. match, which formed part of the series for the Crosfield Cup, was`played on Saturday on the green of the Lindley Club, Huddersfield, in chowery weather, on a very satisfactory green, and before a good number of spectators. Some keen play was witnessed, especially after Yorksbirp had gained the lead at the end of the fifteenth game. From that point Yorkshire were never headed f and they ran out - winners by 485 points to Lancabhire and Cheshire 922. _ .</p>
        <p>Though the Tykes won by 63, they lose on the agreate by six chalks, for the Lancastrians won at Urrnston by 69. Yorkshire. Lancashire &amp; Cheshire. W Spencer, Act.-Pres. e 12 JW 0 Coombs, A-Pres 21 W Kitspn, Vice-Pres.— 8 B Williamson, V-Press 21 F Booth, Punch 80w1... 21 G Holbrk, War Rylnds 14 F Eastwood, Brighouse 21 Arnold, jun., Didsbury 18 J Stead, Dalton Liberal 6 T Ellison, War Cemt'y 21 J Hirst, Spen Victoria 21 H Dawsou,lrlins-o-liC 11 J Tomlinson, Clifton —. 16 H Clark, George H Milnes, Dewsbury Pk 21 II Connolly,Urmston V 14 A Jagger, Punch Bowl 21 A Scott, Warrington C 17 H Heaton, Lockwood ... 21 J Westhead,H'ro'rh'y C 17 W Mitchell, Dalton Lib 18 C W Smitb,Pndltn Bel 21 W Peel, Waterloo J H flolroyd, Lindley G F Dickenso' n Halifax 21 G W Coraer,Ld Nelson 20 J West, Taylor' Hill G P Thewlis,Taylor Hill 21 T Glover, Leigh Ely... 17 C Dyson,Deighton &amp;S 2l II Banks, Lr Broughton 10 G Taylor, Punch Bowl l9 TB Burgess,Wingtn Pk 21 W Oldbam,PaylorHill 2l WBuckley,Trlms-o-H C 15 C Stead, Waterloo 2l E Davn'prt, Pndltn 811 A Shaw, Lindley 2l IA, Gleave, W'gton B H 18 W Brook, Dalton Lib. Jas Garthwaite, Dalton L2l G Ball, jun. W'gton C. 9 L Brown, Ossett 2l H Harrison, Leigh Rly 16 E Carter, Spoa Vie. W Lodge, Dalton Lib.... 21 S Sackville, Swinton S 15</p>
