      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1908-08-01_WidnesExaminer_art0114" n="art0114">
        <head>APPLETON RIFLE CLUB.</head>
        <p>APPLETON RIFLE CLUB.</p>
        <p>Monthly Prize Competitions.</p>
        <p>The third of the series of five monthly competitions was held at the Range last Saturday, when there was a moderate attendance. The finnhtful condition of the weather probably prevented others attending and in fact, during the afternoon the competitors were driven to shelter by the heavy rain storm. All the com- petitions were fired with rainature rifles at 100-yards range, under Risley conditions. The following scores were made:—</p>
        <p>Open Sweepstakes. Seven shots. 3inch bull's eye. Possible 35. J. Sankey 3l , • R. Bennett (tle 14) C. P. Day (tie 12) 29 , F. M. Cowley 27 J. Towers G. P. Greenway l7 Members' Stakes. . Five shots Cinch hull's eye ; five shots disappearing figure. Possible, 40. J. Sankey 3B C. P. Day E Pollard 36 F. M. Cowley 32 I. 8r0ady...... 3O R. Bennett G. P. Greenway 2O J. Towers 25 Tyro Stakes. , Seven shotS 6-inch bull's eye target. Possible 35., V. Plinston 29 G. P. Greenway 2B The following have won " Rifleman's Certificates" during July, 114 points being required out of a possible 130.</p>
        <p>F. M. Cowley HG A. Down</p>
