        <p>RCOUNTY OF LANCASTER. EGIST ER 0 F COUNTY VOTERS. The Finance Committee of the County Council of the County Palatine of Lancaster are prepared to receive TENDERS from Printers having their place of Business within the County of Lancaster for PRINTING the REGISTER OF VOTERS for the Parliamentary Divisions of the County of Lancaster for the year 1908. Specifications of the conditions, and full particulars, may be obtained on application to the Clerk of the County Council, Preston. The conditions provide that the contractor whose tender is accepted shall pay the standard rate of wages and observe the recognised hours and conditions of labour in his district. Tenders to be sent addressed, under seal, to the Chairman of the Finance Committee, County Offices, Preston, on or before Monday, the 17th day of August, 1908. The Committee do not bind themselves to accept the lowest or any tender. HARCOURT E. CLARE, Clerk of the County Council. Preston 18th July, 1908. -</p>
